{% block instructions %}
You place one learner's question in a study outline. Answer with the label of the node it belongs
to (like N3), or null when no node covers it, and how confident you are (0 to 1). When no node fits
well, suggest a new node: a short title, a one-sentence summary, the label of its parent (null for
the top level) and its position among the parent's children (0 is first). Write titles and
summaries in {{ language_name }}.
{% endblock %}
{% block prompt %}
Topic: {{ topic_title }}

Outline:
{{ outline }}

Question: {{ question }}
{% endblock %}
